So it is explicit in tractate Keritot 22b: Rava said, "From the words of both we learn that a definite guilt-offering does not require prior knowledge." And Rambam's words in Hilchot Shegagot chapter 9, law 10, are puzzling; and what the Kesef Mishneh wrote—that it is a dispute between Rabbi Yishmael and Rabbi Akiva—follows Rashi, and that is against Rava's words cited above; see Tosafot Shabbat 72b, <i>s.v.</i> "man de'amar." And Magen Avraham reconciles the Tur's words so that the Tur is not difficult from Rambam's words, unlike Acharonim who wrote that Magen Avraham was unaware of Rambam's words:
